Masflex Non-Stick Crepe Pan makes mastering crepes easier for everybody! It features a heavy gauge aluminum base with a non-stick coating and a heat-resistant bakelite handle. Each pan comes with a free wooden spreader for making perfect crepes each time.
&#xD;
&#xD;
Heavy gauge aluminum&#xD;
Non-stick coating&#xD;
Heat-resistant riveted bakelite handle&#xD;
Induction-compatible bottom&#xD;
Works on all stovetops: Induction, Gas, Electric, Ceramic, etc.&#xD;
Ideal for healthy cooking&#xD;
Heats up quickly and evenly&#xD;
Easy to clean&#xD;
&#xD;
Size:&#xA0;26 cm
&#xD;
Care Instructions:
&#xD;
&#xD;
Before the first use, wash, rinse, and dry the cookware thoroughly.&#xD;
Condition the coating by wiping the cooking surface with an ample amount of cooking oil. Then, heat the cookware for a couple of minutes. After it cools, clean it with a soft cloth and soapy water. This will prolong the life of the non-stick coating.&#xD;
Never heat an empty cookware or allow it to boil dry.&#xD;
Always cook using LOW to MEDIUM heat. The persistent use of high heat causes staining and damage to the cookware and will void the warranty&#xD;
Do not use sharp objects like knives, forks, and metal spoons with sharp edges.&#xD;
Use only wooden, nylon, plastic, and silicone utensils recommended for non-stick cookware.&#xD;
Clean using a delicate sponge and avoid using abrasive cleaners and scouring pads. Don't use a hard or metal scrubber for cleaning. Use liquid detergent, not hard detergent. If anything sticks on the cookware, don't rub it forcefully. Keep water in the cookware for some time and clean it with soapy water.&#xD;
For a longer life span, allow the cookware to cool before washing.&#xD;
Always wash the cookware after each use with warm soapy water, rinse, and dry immediately.&#xD;
Stack the cookware together properly to avoid scratches.&#xD;

