For Best Candle Burning: Trim candle wick to 1/4" (6mm) prior to lighting and before every additional use.
&#xD;
The first burn is most important, and should be just under four hours, enabling the top layer of wax to liquefy to the edge of the glass. This prevents "memory rings" and "tunneling," ensuring full consumption of the wax through the life of the candle.
&#xD;
Warning: To prevent fire, burn candle within sight. Never burn candle on or near anything that can catch fire. Keep away from children and pets. Keep out of drafts. Place candle on stable heat resistant surface. Remove all packaging material before lighting. Trim wick to 1/4 inch (6mm) prior to lighting and before every additional use. Keep wick trimmings, matches and other debris clear from wax pool. Never Burn more than four hours at a time. Always leave at least 20cm (7.87in) between candles. If flame smokes or if candle begins to soot, extinguish, trim wick, and relight. Container will be hot when candle is lit. Stop use when 1/4 inch (6mm) of wax remains. Do not use water to extinguish candle. Ignoring these warnings may lead to fire hazard or personal injury.

