For stubborn residue, fill your cookware with warm, soapy water and let it sit for an hour. Then bring your soapy water to boil for 10 to 15 minutes. Let the water cool to the touch before scrubbing out the residue with a nylon scouring pad. Finally, rinse and dry your cookware thoroughly.&#xD;
